libnet: include <netinet/in.h> on android

net_util_md.h builds its SOCKETADDRESS union out of struct sockaddr_in /
sockaddr_in6, but only includes <netdb.h>, <poll.h> and <sys/socket.h>.
glibc's <netdb.h> drags in <netinet/in.h> as a side effect, so the omission
never shows there; bionic's does not, and every libnet source fails:

  net_util_md.h:70:25: error: field has incomplete type 'struct sockaddr_in'
  net_util_md.h:71:25: error: field has incomplete type 'struct sockaddr_in6'

Include the header that actually declares them. Guarded on __ANDROID__ like
termux-packages' 0001-libinet-include-netinet-in.h-for-android-builds, so the
other targets keep the include set upstream tests.

diff --git a/src/java.base/unix/native/libnet/net_util_md.h b/src/java.base/unix/native/libnet/net_util_md.h
--- a/src/java.base/unix/native/libnet/net_util_md.h
+++ b/src/java.base/unix/native/libnet/net_util_md.h
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@
 #ifndef NET_UTILS_MD_H
 #define NET_UTILS_MD_H
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#include <netinet/in.h>
+#endif
 #include <netdb.h>
 #include <poll.h>
 #include <sys/socket.h>
